 "result_text": "I changed `Session.loadConfigFiles` in `nose2/session.py` so that `-c tox.ini` is read as an ini file again. I haven't run the tests or tried your `nose2 -c tox.ini --junit-xml` command.\n\nv0.15.0 only read files ending in `.cfg` as ini, and treated files ending in `pyproject.toml` as TOML. Any other name, including `tox.ini`, was silently skipped. Your `[unittest] plugins` section was therefore never loaded, so `--junit-xml` was unrecognized.\n\nNow any filename ending in `.toml` is parsed as TOML, and every other filename is read as ini. Because the TOML check is now `.toml` instead of `pyproject.toml`, a TOML file with another name is also parsed as TOML. Unlike before, it is still parsed if it has no `[tool.nose2]` table, but nothing is loaded from it in that case.",
